  "explicit_non_claims": [
    "This module does not authenticate tenant IDs; the caller must bind tenant principal IDs to authenticated identities.",
    "This module reuses the evidence-bound resource inventory validator from the existing resource allocator and does not create a second resource inventory engine.",
    "Tenant-weighted progressive filling is not a global maximum-sum-rate optimizer.",
    "The bounded integer oracle fixture proves agreement only for its explicitly enumerated small topologies, not general LP optimality.",
    "No claim is made that tenant weights, flow weights or path split weights are fair without an externally justified policy.",
    "No rate is allocated on a path whose required resource evidence is unknown, stale, incomplete, low-confidence or topology-mismatched.",
    "The input resource snapshot digest is caller-computed and echoed, not independently authenticated by this module.",
    "No route, SIM/eSIM, qdisc, congestion-control or radio actuation is performed.",
    "CAKE and fq_codel are queue-management comparators, not equivalent tenant/path allocation algorithms.",
    "No namespace, hardware or field performance result is claimed by deterministic unit tests.",
    "The allocator does not guarantee a globally optimal path split under arbitrary path/resource incidence; it is bounded and deterministic.",
    "The allocator does not implement packet ordering, receiver reassembly or transport congestion control.",
    "A successful allocation report is a plan under one frozen resource snapshot, not proof that the network actually delivered that rate."
  ]
